#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:5
#: 296c236e7503450b88344b4666e34181
msgid "Traditional Helicopter – Tailrotor Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:7
#: 7e9df63cd49d49eeac43b52b80ddb50d
msgid "There are several ways for controlling the tailrotor to maintain yaw stabilization and provide yaw control, and each have a unique setup.  The :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` parameter is used to specify method for controlling the tailrotor.  A list of available tail types is given below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:9
#: 099361c2700743228bd928433e6b38de
msgid "Servo Only: ArduPilot will supply the tail rotor stabilization like a tail rotor gyro and control the pitch of the tail rotor blades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:10
#: 6a974e7be30348d1b79e59eb79ce5a15
msgid "Servo with External Gyro: ArduPilot will output yaw demands without direct yaw attitude stabilization which is provided via an external gyro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:11
#: 1c0b6c53d1bb4d5eb311d6cdadbc3bb0
msgid "Direct Drive Variable Pitch (DDVP): Instead of the tail rotor being driven from the main rotor via mechanical coupling as in the above cases, an electric motor is used with motor controlled(ramp up/down, operating point) by ArduPilot. Main yaw control is via tail blade pitch servo, as above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:12
#: fdf2ef6380134d8388c93f9fafb01d3b
msgid "Direct Drive Fixed Pitch Clockwise (DDFP CW): Tail rotor is driven by a motor whose ESC is controlled by ArduPilot to maintain yaw stability and yaw direction. Used with clockwise rotating main rotors, when viewed from above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:13
#: a8383e774a9e4f55b763178678ab5ed6
msgid "Direct Drive Fixed Pitch Counter-Clockwise (DDFP CCW): Tail rotor driven by a motor whose ESC is controlled by ArudPilot to maintain yaw stability and yaw direction. Used with counter-clockwise rotating main rotors, when viewed from above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:17
#: 296aca3edc174866b199e04789eabc1e
msgid "Tailrotor Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:20
#: c3d83f99f29d400b9ba1e9df38c6bc25
msgid "Servo Only :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:22
#: 6c0692fe7d55482ea59f61ed46455bc5
msgid "The Servo Only tail type uses a servo connected to an autopilot output whose ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` is selected as ``Motor4`` to control the tailrotor pitch slider.  The tailrotor speed is controlled by a physical connection (tailrotor shaft or belt) to the engine and main shaft. Depending on your servo setup and mechanical throws, set the ``SERVOx_MIN``, ``SERVOx_MAX``, and ``SERVOx_REVERSED`` parameter values.  Setting the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` is discussed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:24
#: 23590dad17a848ca99c2487a020b0074
msgid "Be sure to check the direction of operation of the Tail Servo. Move the rudder stick and notice the change in tail rotor pitch. Be sure that its increase or decrease of pitch is such that the change in thrust will result in the desired direction of movement. If not, reverse the servo direction with the ``SERVOx_REVERSED`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:27
#: ffa07aa6d64d482c8d9f29185446bded
msgid "Servo with External Gyro :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:29
#: f0fb6af02577453a967a4fe103134d97
msgid "Instead of ArduPilot controlling both the desired yaw rate and stability, this option relies on an external gyro for stabilization. A servo is still used to input yaw rate demands to the tail and its setup as above, for the Servo Only case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:31
#: 65bbf15f4c59451eb4ea93ab392fbd28
msgid "The external gyro gain can be set by the ``H_GYR_GAIN`` parameter using the autopilot's \"Motor7\" output function,``SERVOx_FUNCTION``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:33
#: 69d38e5aa3714ebc9a25b15c9a1fae1f
msgid "In ACRO mode, this gain can be changed to the value of the ``H_GYR_GAIN_ACRO`` parameter, if non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:36
#: eae5a81ee9d9486ca5836b996783fa4b
msgid "Direct Drive Variable Pitch :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:38
#: b94aa23b9d184eeb890fb84b0bd268d9
msgid "The Direct Drive Variable Pitch (DDVP) tail type uses a separate tail motor with a variable pitch propeller.  A separate servo is used to control the tailrotor pitch.  The setup of the servo is similar to the servo only tail type. ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` \"Motor4\" is assigned to the output number that corresponds to the servo channel the tailrotor servo is physically connected (defaults to output 4).  For the tail motor, the \"HeliTailRSC\" (\"32\") is assigned to the motor/servo channel to which the tail motor ESC is physically connected (defaults to output 7)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:40
#: e7871e96fcf74c498299666e22052f6f
msgid "The range of the motor ESC is controlled by its output's ``SERVOx_MIN/MAX`` parameters and ArduPilot will ramp it output up or down, as appropriate, to its normal operating value set by the :ref:`H_TAIL_SPEED<H_TAIL_SPEED>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:43
#: bf0718f562b44838bf743da89df5b9da
msgid "Direct Drive Fixed Pitch :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 3 or 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:45
#: 5de76b4686a5462b8dd4b9fa1a41a79d
msgid "The Direct Drive Fixed Pitch (DDFP) tail type uses a fixed pitch tail rotor and separate motor. The stabilization and yaw is controlled by the speed of this motor. It has two options: one where the main rotor rotates clockwise when viewed from above and the other where the main rotor rotates counter-clockwise when viewed from above.  Be sure to select the DDFP tail type for the main rotor rotation.  In this case, the control of tailrotor thrust is accomplished through tailrotor speed since it is a fixed pitch propeller. The ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` of \"36\" (Motor4) should be assigned to the servo channel to which the tailrotor ESC is physically connected.  On new DDFP setups it is suggested to set ``H_DDFP_THST_EXPO`` to .65 as a starting point.  This will be a good enough thrust expo for most aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:47
#: 13e8f8248ffc489eb17d047f630e883e
msgid "There are several parameters that provide the ability to linearize the thrust produced by the tail rotor motor and therefore provide better control:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:49
#: 60fe5d07d6f94fe6bf61c41b6c133f55
msgid ":ref:`H_DDFP_THST_EXPO<H_DDFP_THST_EXPO>` - Tail rotor DDFP motor thrust curve exponent (0.0 for linear to 1.0 for second order curve). A suggested starting point for tuning this parameter is .65 and will often give better better results than the default. Default = 0 (for legacy compatibility reason)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:50
#: f0f2772591cd40f9812a1da0138148f9
msgid ":ref:`H_DDFP_SPIN_MIN<H_DDFP_SPIN_MIN>` - Point at which the DDFP motor thrust starts expressed as a number from 0 to 1 in the entire output range.  Default = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:51
#: 1c5d5f759f9f4c6ba55f23010617b468
msgid ":ref:`H_DDFP_SPIN_MAX<H_DDFP_SPIN_MAX>` - Point at which the DDFP motor thrust saturates expressed as a number from 0 to 1 in the entire output range. Default = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:52
#: 224ec0b5af98410081da9e715af0a3eb
msgid ":ref:`H_DDFP_BAT_IDX<H_DDFP_BAT_IDX>` - Index of battery to be used for voltage compensation. Default = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:53
#: 3b5b8052f27d4170ad795eed6fe63baf
msgid ":ref:`H_DDFP_BAT_V_MAX<H_DDFP_BAT_V_MAX>` - Battery voltage compensation maximum voltage (voltage above this will have no additional scaling effect on thrust). Recommend 4.2 * cell count, 0 = Disabled. Default = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:54
#: 1cb4b7d69f64445f937ae14d79fe7c21
msgid ":ref:`H_DDFP_BAT_V_MIN<H_DDFP_BAT_V_MIN>` - Battery voltage compensation minimum voltage (voltage below this will have no additional scaling effect on thrust). Recommend 3.3 * cell count, 0 = Disabled. Default = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:56
#: 905920f5d9b8456992bf488213b5f716
msgid "These parameters should be set similarly to how Copter's motor scaling parameterss are setup. See :ref:`Copters Motor Thrust Scaling <motor-thrust-scaling>` document for more information."
msgstr ""

